Given square matrix

 M = \left[ {\matrix{ 0 & 1 & a  \cr 1 & 2 & 3  \cr 3 & b & 1  \cr

} } \right] 

and adj  (M) = \left[ {\matrix{ { - 1} & 1 & { - 1}  \cr 8 & { - 6} & 2  \cr { - 5} & 3 & { - 1}  \cr

} } \right] 

$\because$ |adj (M)| = |M|^{2} =  \left[ {\matrix{
   { - 1} & 1 & { - 1}  \cr 
   8 & { - 6} & 2  \cr 
   { - 5} & 3 & { - 1}  \cr 

} } \right] 

$\Rightarrow |M{|^2} =  - 1(6 - 6) - 1( - 8 + 10) - 1(24 - 30) =  - 2 + 6 = 4 \Rightarrow |M| =  \pm 2 \therefore$ det (adj $M^{2}$) = $|{M^2}{|^2} = |M{|^4} = 16$

As we know A(adj A) = |A| I

$\Rightarrow$ M = |M| (adj M)^{-1} ....(i)

$\because$ (adj M)^{-1} =  {1 \over {|adj\,M|}}{\left[ {\matrix{
   0 & { - 2} & { - 6}  \cr 
   { - 2} & { - 4} & { - 2}  \cr 
   { - 4} & { - 6} & { - 2}  \cr 

} } \right]^T} 

=  \frac{1}{4}\left[ {\matrix{ 0 & { - 2} & { - 4}  \cr { - 2} & { - 4} & { - 6}  \cr { - 6} & { - 2} & { - 2}  \cr

} } \right] 

So \left[ {\matrix{ 0 & 1 & a  \cr 1 & 2 & 3  \cr 3 & b & 1  \cr

 } } \right] = {{|M|} \over 4}\left[ {\matrix{
